      "script": "BUS 166\nWe are heading from Ulu towards Ulu.\nYou won’t find a bus stop with this name. It is our magical journey that carries the name.\nStay on board or prepare to wander a trail.\n\nMYNAS (chatting)\nTHE RECLAIMED ARCHIVE\nUlu—in Malay—means upstream, remote, a place slightly out of sight.\n(a Malay voice explains)\n(Malay voice)\nHulu hilir—\nupstream, downstream.\nBack and forth.\n\nMYNA 1&2 (imitating the Archive)\nhulu hilir\nhulu hilir\n\nMYNA 1\nThe Archive talking so chim (profound) again. Upstream, downstream... I just follow my nose.\n\nMYNA 2\nI just follow the smell.\nCurry puff.\nWaste.\nBus fumes.\n\nMYNA 1\nThen heat.\nPanas. Panas.\n\nMYNA 2\nThen noise.",
      "notes": [
        "Spoken text follows the recording; unspoken stage directions and explanatory translations are omitted."
      ],
